      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.  retrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.  A crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
